  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID funded Conservation and Sustainable Management Partnership (CARPE Partnership in Salonga National Park)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Central Africa Regional):  Salonga National Park in the heart of the Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC) is the largest forested national park in Africa, larger than the state of Maryland, and the most significant stronghold for the country&apos;s endemic bonobo population. It is also home to one of the largest remaining populations of forest elephants in the DRC...USAID FY 2022 funds will support the conservation and sustainable management of Salonga National Park. The primary objective is to establish delegated authority for the management of the park with a private sector partner through a 10-year agreement expected to establish strong long-term management of this important protected area. This activity will leverage substantial private financial and technical resources from outside the country with the objective of building the capacity of park management and developing sustainable development opportunities for the surrounding population. It will establish an approach to human rights and social safeguards developed in partnership with the Government of the DRC...This activity will contribute to advancing U.S. government priorities in Central Africa designed to maintain the ecological integrity of the humid forest ecosystem of the Congo Basin, which is vital to regional stability, a U.S. foreign policy priority. It contributes to Joint Strategic Priority Strategic Objective 2.2: (Promote healthy, educated and productive populations in partner countries to drive inclusive and sustainable development, open new markets and support U.S. prosperity and security objectives) by protecting natural resources critical to long term, sustainable growth, and food and water security.</narrative>
  </description>
